r-worker compute", "text": "The anomaly-detection kernel that runs inside one worker's own memory, and whether sharded detection is even accurate enough to ship.\nListed child items: Choose a streaming-friendly anomaly algorithm, Measure the per-invocation compute budget, Build and benchmark the SIMD kernel, Validate accuracy against a single-machine baseline.", "layer": 1, "children": ["kernel-algo", "spike-timebudget", "kernel-impl", "kernel-accuracy"], "covers_ref": true, "covers_why": "Algorithm choice, implementation and an accuracy check against a real baseline cover picking, building and validating the kernel.", "atomic_ref": false, "owner_role": "ml-eng", "risk_reason": null, "status": null, "gate": false, "phase": null, "answers": {"atomic": {"type": "noul", "noul": 0.02}, "covers": {"type": "noul", "noul": 0.92}}, "grade": {"atomic_p": 0.02, "atomic_correct": true, "covers_p": 0.92, "covers_correct": true}}, {"id": "sys-orch", "parent": "root", "kind": "group", "title": "Cross-worker exchange", "text": "Coordinating many independent workers and moving only the anomalous deltas between them, since there is no shared memory to pass full results through.\nListed child items: Choose the coordination primitive, Define the delta format, Define the reduce step, Build dispatch and collect.", "layer": 1, "children": ["orch-primitive", "orch-delta", "orch-reduce", "orch-impl"], "covers_ref": true, "covers_why": "Coordination primitive, delta format, reduce step and the implementation that builds them cover moving deltas between workers.", "atomic_ref": false, "owner_role": "platform-eng", "risk_reason": null, "status": null, "gate": false, "phase": null, "answers": {"atomic": {"type": "noul", "noul": 0.2}, "covers": {"type": "noul", "noul": 0.45}}, "grade": {"atomic_p": 0.2, "atomic_correct": true, "covers_p": 0.45, "covers_correct": false}}, {"id": "sys-train", "parent": "root", "kind": "group", "title": "Model state and training", "text": "Accumulating a trained m