type": "noul", "noul": 0.5933067821210363}}, "grade": {"atomic_p": 0.6012758362688174}}, {"id": "sys-platform", "parent": "root", "kind": "group", "title": "Platform limits", "text": "What Cloudflare's Workers platform actually gives you, measured or looked up, before anything else is sized against it.\nListed child items: Measure the per-isolate memory ceiling, Measure worker-to-worker transfer, Confirm WASM SIMD availability, Measure concurrency and fan-out ceilings, Measure exchange bandwidth and price.", "layer": 1, "children": ["spike-memcap", "spike-sharedmem", "feas-simd", "feas-fanout", "feas-netcost"], "covers_ref": true, "covers_why": "Memory ceiling, shared memory, SIMD availability, fan-out and exchange cost are the five concrete platform facts the rest of the architecture depends on.", "atomic_ref": false, "owner_role": "platform-eng", "risk_reason": null, "status": null, "gate": false, "phase": null, "answers": {"atomic": {"type": "noul", "noul": 0.6343349482600732}, "covers": {"type": "noul", "noul": 0.6277817540734058}}, "grade": {"atomic_p": 0.6343349482600732, "atomic_correct": false, "covers_p": 0.6277817540734058, "covers_correct": true}}, {"id": "sys-ingest", "parent": "root", "kind": "group", "title": "Ingest and sharding", "text": "Getting the source dataset in and split into per-worker chunks that fit inside the platform's real limits.\nListed child items: Choose where the source dataset lives, Size the per-worker chunk, Build the shard loader.", "layer": 1, "children": ["ingest-source", "ingest-chunk", "ingest-loader"], "covers_ref": true, "covers_why": "Source, chunk size and the loader that builds on them fully cover getting data from source to worker.", "atomic_ref": false, "owner_role": "data-eng", "risk_reason": null, "status": null, "gate": false, "phase": null, "answers": {"atomic": {"type": "noul", "noul": 0.7329761032180206}, "covers": {"type": "noul", "noul": 0.6732259390273267}}, "grade": {"atomic_p": 0.7329761032180206, "atomic_correct": false, "covers_p": 0.6732259390273267, "covers_correct": true}}, {"id": "sys-kernel", "parent": "root", "kind": "group", "title": "Per-worker compute", "text": "The anomaly-detection kernel that runs inside one worker's own memory, and whether sharded detection is even accurate enough to ship.\nListed child items: Choose a streaming-friendly anomaly algorithm, Measure the per-invocation compute budget, Build and benchmark the SIMD kernel, Validate accuracy against a single-machine baseline.", "layer": 1, "children": ["kernel-algo", "spike-timebudget", "kernel-impl", "kernel-accuracy"], "covers_ref": true, "covers_why": "Algorithm choice, implementation and an accuracy check against a real baseline cover picking, building and validating the kernel.", "atomic_ref": false, "owner_role": "ml-eng", "risk_reason": null, "status": null, "gate": false, "phase": null, "answers": {"atomic": {"type": "noul", "noul": 0.6445546090508059}, "covers": {"type": "noul", "noul": 0.6276268195615078}}, "grade": {"atomic_p": 0.6445546090508059, "atomic_correct": false, "covers_p": 0.6276268195615078, "covers_correct": true}}, {"id": "sys-orch", "parent": "root", "kind": "group", "title": "Cross-worker exchange", "text": "Coordinating many independent workers and moving only the anomalous deltas between them, since there is no shared memory to pass full results through.\nListed child items: Choose the coordination primitive, Define the delta format, Define the reduce step, Build dispatch and collect.", "layer": 1, "children": ["orch-primitive", "orch-delta", "orch-reduce", "orch-impl"], "covers_ref": true, "covers_why": "Coordination primitive, delta format, reduce step and the implementation that builds them cover moving deltas between workers.", "atomic_ref": false, "owner_role": "platform-eng", "risk_reason": null, "status": null, "gate": false, "phase": null, "answers": {"atomic": {"type": "noul", "noul": 0.669582698426968}, "covers": {"type": "noul", "noul": 0.623511186551438}}, "grade": {"atomic_p": 0.669582698426968, "atomic_correct": false, "covers_p": 0.623511186551438, "covers_correct": true}}, {"id": "sys-train", "parent": "root", "kind": "group", "title": "Model state and training", "text": "Accumulating a trained model from a stream of deltas across many short-lived invocations, and persisting the running state between them.\nListed child items: Choose where accumulating state lives, Confirm the model supports incremental updates, Build state accumulation and reload.", "layer": 1, "children": ["train-state", "train-online", "train-impl"], "covers_ref": false, "covers_why": "Where state lives and whether the model updates incrementally are two real questions, but neither addresses what happens when several workers finish at the same moment and all try to write the accumulated state. Last-write-wins silently loses updates; a single serialising writer becomes a bottleneck for a design whose whole premise is many workers training at once. That is a real hole, and nothing else in this plan fills it.", "atomic_ref": false, "owner_role": "ml-eng", "risk_reason": null, "status": null, "gate": false, "phase": null, "answers": {"atomic": {"type": "noul", "noul": 0.6677095606656237}, "covers": {"type": "noul", "noul": 0.6194460161436681}}, "grade": {"atomic_p": 0.6677095606656237, "atomic_correct": false, "covers_p": 0.6194460161436681, "covers_correct": false}}, {"id": "sys-ops", "parent": "root", "kind": "group", "title": "Correctness, operations and launch", "text": "What a working prototype still needs before it can run unattended: failure handling, observability, a real cost figure, and a launch path. Missing from the pitch as given.\nListed child items: Handle worker failure, Add per-pass observability, Build a real cost projection, Run end-to-end at target scale, Deploy and launch.", "layer": 1, "children": ["ops-failure", "ops-observability", "ops-costmodel", "ops-e2e", "ops-launch"], "covers_ref": true, "covers_why": "Failure han